From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: stop polling the decoder device on error

V4L2Decoder's error state is final, and serviceDeviceTask() returns at
once in it, before it dequeues buffers or events. Polling continues
until the component stops or releases the decoder. A SOURCE_CHANGE
event that is pending when the error occurs, or that the driver sends
afterwards for input it already holds, is then never dequeued: poll()
keeps returning POLLPRI and the poll thread and the decoder thread keep
each other busy, for as long as the client takes to release the codec.

Stop polling in onError(). Nothing is lost, since the decoder ignores
the device from then on; flush() does nothing in the error state, so
polling is not restarted, and the destructor's stopPolling() call does
nothing when polling has already stopped.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
index 31111ea..be6fbb9 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Decoder.cpp
@@ -1077,6 +1077,10 @@ void V4L2Decoder::onError() {
     ALOGV("%s()", __func__);
     ALOG_ASSERT(mTaskRunner->RunsTasksInCurrentSequence());
 
+    // The error state is final and serviceDeviceTask() ignores the device in it. A pending
+    // SOURCE_CHANGE event would never be dequeued and keep poll() returning POLLPRI until the
+    // decoder is destroyed.
+    if (mDevice) mDevice->stopPolling();
     setState(State::Error);
     mErrorCb.Run();
 }
